From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:18:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(entities): resolve and order Bedrock passenger links

A remove-entity packet can arrive before the related link update. Keep vehicle passenger lists in sync when actors despawn, and prune unknown passengers before encoding Java passenger packets so bulk removals do not disconnect the client. Also clear the local mount state when its vehicle disappears.

Resolve links received before either actor spawns, preserve rider ordering, and emit passenger updates after removal or dismount. This keeps Java vehicle state consistent across Bedrock packet orderings.

On unlink or vehicle removal, seed the player position from the vehicle and schedule a Java position correction. This prevents stale boarding coordinates and riding offsets after dismount.
